        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "STANDALONE H3 CHECKPOINT UPSCALE\n\n1. Open Checkpoint Manager and select the saved run.\n2. Select a COMPLETE branch, then click Load selected branch. The Plan at left is replaced with that exact saved branch.\n3. Choose a unique profile in Upscale Adapter. start_clip=1/end_clip=0 processes all scenes.\n4. Queue. Each HQ scene is saved before the loop advances; Merger writes under output/h3_chains/<run>/upscaled/<profile>/final/.\n\nsave_latent is OFF by default. The sampler latent is still carried transiently between scenes, but only the small audio/assembly checkpoint is persisted. Enable it if you need to reopen the HQ latent later.\n\nFor source_track plans, connect the original full AUDIO to Adapter/Merger if validation requests it."
      ],
      "title": "HOW TO RUN"
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        1500,
        750
      ],
      "size": [
        1200,
        540
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 23,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "REQUIRES\nhttps://github.com/Tr1dae/ComfyUI-MiniMaxH3_LatentUpscaler\nIts learned path also uses the sibling Mamad8 architecture pack and downloads the selected learned checkpoint on first use.\n\nThe graph uses the saved denoised x0 when present, otherwise the terminal sampler latent. Combined upscales the JOINT H3 AV latent, re-noises only video, locks pass-1 audio at audio_denoise=0, and returns resized conditioning. The Guider is rebuilt from that returned conditioning.\n\nDefaults: fixed learned 2x, staggered 4-step pass at denoise 0.45, Euler, no latent blur or sharpen. Adjust the pass-2 controls after validating one short profile. This workflow rebuilds T2VA text conditioning from the saved prompt; reference-heavy Ref2VA recipes may need their original reference conditioning wired into the backend body."
      ],
      "title": "DEPENDENCY / PASS-2 NOTES"
    }
  ],
